{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Who is like the wise.</b> There is a word that draws itself and another with it, like the word אל in קצף אל תוכיח (rebuke with wrath), יחי ראובן ואל ימות (let Reuben live and not die), מתן בסתר יכפה אף (a gift in secret conceals anger), and likewise one may find a word drawing another after it, like מאל אביך ויעזרך (from the El of your father and He will help you), ואת שדי (and Shaddai), ומאת שדי (and from Shaddai) — this is the matter of the verse above: מידי אביר יעקב (from the hands of the Mighty One of Jacob), מאל אביך והוא יעזרך (from the El of your father and He will help you always). The Gaon [Saadia] said its meaning is: I will ask of the El of your father and He will help you, and according to both interpretations a mem must be added before et. Likewise מישרים אהבוך (the upright love you), ומישרים (and upright) is an adjective of wine, and like it יתהלך במישרים (he walks uprightly), and כיין הטוב הולך לדודי למישרים (like good wine going to my beloved uprightly). And אהבוך (love you) returns upon the maidens mentioned in the first verse. And likewise מי כהחכם ומי כיודע פשר דבר (who is like the wise and who knows the interpretation of a matter). It is possible that the meaning of מי כהחכם is: who is he that knows the interpretation of a matter. The word פשר (interpretation) belongs to the Aramaic family, and the meaning is: why do people busy themselves to devise many calculations that do not profit, and there is none who is on a straight path like the wise man who seeks wisdom and inquires to know the interpretation of every matter — what purpose there is in it and why it is so. And it is possible that פשר is the reverse, its final letter turned inside out, from כי לא פורש (for it was not interpreted). And the meaning of חכמת אדם תאיר פניו (a man's wisdom illuminates his face): it places light in his face, and the meaning is, it removes anger, as in באור פני מלך חיים (the brightening of the king's face is life)." "<b>And the meaning of \"and the boldness of his face is hated\" (ועז פניו ישונא).</b> Turn away the boldness of face from yourself, for wisdom produces humility, for when the soul overcomes the spirit, anger and boldness of brow depart."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The phrase כי לא פורש (for it was not interpreted) is Daniel 5:12/5:16. Ibn Ezra argues that פשר is an inversion of פרש (same root letters reversed). Rendered literally without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:29.970479713Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}